      "message": "`slugify` now transliterates accented letters: `café` becomes `cafe`, and `Crème Brûlée` becomes `creme-brulee`. All three tests in `tests/test_core.py` pass, including a new test for the accented case.\n\nThe fix is in `slug/core.py`. The old loop silently dropped any non-ASCII letter via `elif ch.isalpha(): continue`. Now the input is decomposed with Unicode NFKD and combining marks are stripped before the loop, so accents fall away and the base letters survive.\n\nLimitations:\n- Letters that don't decompose into a base letter are still dropped: `ø`, `ß`, `æ`, `ł`, and non-Latin scripts such as CJK. Handling those needs an explicit mapping table. I didn't add one, since you asked for accent transliteration.\n- I added the accented-letter test to `tests/test_core.py`. That file was already in scope for running tests, so this is the only change outside `slug/core.py`.\n\nI haven't committed anything.",
